    {
      "title": "BAN stun AUS by 9 wickets, seal historic first Test win on Australian soil",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/ban-stun-aus-by-9-wickets-seal-historic-first-test-win-on-australian-soil-126081600148_1.html",
      "description": "Bangladesh completed a stunning nine-wicket victory over Australia in the first test on Sunday, securing its first win on Australian soil and only its second victory over the top-ranked Australia.\nAfter making a vital half-century in Bangladesh's first innings, Mehidy Hasan Miraz took five wickets in Australia's second innings to restrict the hosts to a lead of just 56 runs, before Australia was bowled out for 284 midway through the afternoon session at Darwin's Marrara Oval.\nCameron Green scored his third test century, and his first in Australia, making a composed 104 from 201 balls to lead Australia's resistance and give Bangladesh a modest target.\nBangladesh suffered some early nerves when Josh Hazlewood (1-5) dismissed first-innings centurion Tanzid Hasan for a duck, but Shadman Islam (25 not out) and Mominul Haque (30 not out) held their composure to chase down the target in 14.2 overs sparking wild celebrations within the contingent of Bangladesh fans seated behind the team's",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-08-16T06:09:18"
    },
    {
      "title": "Historic day for Bangladesh! Tigers seal maiden Test win in Australia",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/bangladesh-beat-australia-darwin-maiden-test-win-mehidy-hasan-miraz-highlights-full-scorecard-126081600121_1.html",
      "description": "Bangladesh scripted history in Darwin with their maiden Test win in Australia as Mehidy Hasan Miraz and Hasan Mahmud starred with the ball.",
